  "reasoning": "The patient reports severe stomach pain, constipation for several days, along with nightly headaches and chills. This symptom cluster aligns precisely with Reference [1], which lists stomach pain, bloating, constipation, high fever, and chills, resulting in a diagnosis of typhoid. Typhoid fever characteristically combines gastrointestinal distress (notably constipation in adults) with systemic signs like fever, chills, and headaches. Other potential diagnoses are factually ruled out: gastroesophageal reflux disease and peptic ulcer disease center on acid reflux, heartburn, and food-triggered pain without chills or constipation; malaria features chills and headaches but does not typically cause severe stomach pain and constipation. Thus, the facts uniquely establish typhoid.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]typhoid[/DIAGNOSIS]"
